From a49ea52305a61d204188092422511d1a0f9cd9f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michel JAOUEN <michel.jaouen@st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Dec 2025 15:04:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 899/913] mod/scmi_clock: fix get config to match specification

The specification for clock protocol version 0x3000 says that attributes
field is filled with 0 and config is filled with clock_state.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 2688df49e3787a9eedb9a866a04f16d6ff63b744 mod/scmi_clock: fix get config to match specification]
Change-Id: I1c3708ec1e8fcb66c8d675d2acdb3e56e48e76f9
Signed-off-by: Michel JAOUEN <michel.jaouen@st.com>
---
 .../SCP-firmware/module/scmi_clock/src/mod_scmi_clock.c        | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_clock/src/mod_scmi_clock.c b/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_clock/src/mod_scmi_clock.c
index f97db8043..e9f689904 100644
--- a/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_clock/src/mod_scmi_clock.c
+++ b/core/lib/scmi-server/SCP-firmware/module/scmi_clock/src/mod_scmi_clock.c
@@ -1466,7 +1466,8 @@ static int scmi_clock_config_get_handler(fwk_id_t service_id,
 
         return_values = (struct scmi_clock_config_get_p2a){
             .status = SCMI_SUCCESS,
-            .attributes = clock_state,
+            .attributes = 0,
+            .config = clock_state,
         };
         break;
 
-- 
